    <briefdescription>
<para>Compute live ranges of allocas. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Live ranges are represented as sets of &quot;interesting&quot; instructions, which are defined as instructions that may start or end an alloca&apos;s lifetime. These are:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>lifetime.start and lifetime.end intrinsics</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>first instruction of any basic block Interesting instructions are numbered in the depth-first walk of the CFG, and in the program order inside each basic block. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
